      "writtenOn": "2022-06-14T21:16:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes here, For ITE TCPC as well as for FUSBC TCPC, DRP state - Auto toggle is disabled when nothing is connected. Also, this change will force the state to TC_LOW_POWER_MODE  from tc_unattached_src/snk_run() ( File - common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c ). Now, coming to ITE specific tcpm driver, the low power mode entry function(it83xx_tcpm_enter_low_power_mode) does really nothing , as it is controlled by ITE TCPC clk in deep sleep mode.  So, for ITE specific TCPC port, this change should not really matter. In RVP, P0 is ITE based and P1/P2/P3 is FUSB based. On veryfying with TBT and USB4 connection, both ports seemed to exit low power mode and devices were enumerated fine.",
